{
  "name": "Text colour by value",
  "description": "A text layer colours the numbers inside its text by value, with the chart's band table and highlight. The price line uses bands (typed out of order, so sorting counts) and highlight both: 32 is the lowest, 70 the highest, 66 is past the table. The tie reads 5 9 2 9 2, so the first 9 and the first 2 are marked and the rest keep the layer colour. A single number is both ends and the highest wins. Mixed text colours only its numbers and the units keep the layer colour. The signed line pins a negative, a decimal, and a hyphen after a digit that is not a sign. Highlight on its own leaves the other numbers in the layer colour, merged into the text around them. A rule that rewrites the text and recolours the layer is what the numbers are read from and what the rest of the text keeps. A countdown ignores the keys, a layer with no keys draws one colour, and a layer with a table but One colour draws one colour too. A trailing full stop is read as part of the number but keeps the layer colour, while the dot inside 5.5 stays coloured. Text with no numbers still carries spans, one run in the layer colour, and empty text carries an empty list of spans rather than none.",
